<hr data-start="315" data-end="318">
<h2 data-start="320" data-end="369">ğŸ§  SYSTEM OVERVIEW: <em data-start="343" data-end="369">Narrative Masking Engine</em></h2>
<p data-start="371" data-end="571"><strong data-start="371" data-end="379">Goal</strong>: Transform an existing film into a new <strong data-start="419" data-end="450">tropeological configuration</strong> without changing the raw footage directly â€” or minimally â€” using layered inference, editing, and AI-driven augmentation.</p>
<hr data-start="573" data-end="576">
<h3 data-start="578" data-end="623">ğŸ§± 1. <strong data-start="588" data-end="623">Scene &amp; Structure Decomposition</strong></h3>
<blockquote data-start="625" data-end="676">
<p data-start="627" data-end="676">â€œWhatâ€™s happening, structurally and emotionally?â€</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="678" data-end="743">This layer breaks a film into <em data-start="708" data-end="730">semantic story units</em>, extracting:</p>
<ul data-start="745" data-end="1012">
<li data-start="745" data-end="807">
<p data-start="747" data-end="807"><strong data-start="747" data-end="767">Scene boundaries</strong> (visual cut + narrative beat detection)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="808" data-end="836">
<p data-start="810" data-end="836"><strong data-start="810" data-end="836">Dialogue transcription</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="837" data-end="891">
<p data-start="839" data-end="891"><strong data-start="839" data-end="863">Emotion trajectories</strong> (tone curves, mood vectors)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="892" data-end="949">
<p data-start="894" data-end="949"><strong data-start="894" data-end="923">Character archetype roles</strong> (via behavior + function)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="950" data-end="1012">
<p data-start="952" data-end="1012"><strong data-start="952" data-end="972">Plot scaffolding</strong> (what trope is this moment fulfilling?)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1014" data-end="1023">ğŸ›  Tools:</p>
<ul data-start="1024" data-end="1290">
<li data-start="1024" data-end="1085">
<p data-start="1026" data-end="1085">Scene segmentation: via shot detection (e.g. PySceneDetect)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1086" data-end="1132">
<p data-start="1088" data-end="1132">Dialogue â†’ NLP parsing for intention/context</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1133" data-end="1188">
<p data-start="1135" data-end="1188">Emotion: multimodal sentiment (audio + facial + text)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1189" data-end="1232">
<p data-start="1191" data-end="1232">Archetypes: transformer-based classifiers</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1233" data-end="1290">
<p data-start="1235" data-end="1290">Structural role tagging: LLMs with film grammar prompts</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1292" data-end="1295">
<h3 data-start="1297" data-end="1337">ğŸ¨ 2. <strong data-start="1307" data-end="1337">Genre Mask / Trope Overlay</strong></h3>
<blockquote data-start="1339" data-end="1388">
<p data-start="1341" data-end="1388">â€œWhat kind of film is this trying to be <em data-start="1381" data-end="1386">now</em>?â€</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="1390" data-end="1457">The genre mask is like a <strong data-start="1415" data-end="1446">set of transformation rules</strong>, defining:</p>
<ul data-start="1459" data-end="1835">
<li data-start="1459" data-end="1526">
<p data-start="1461" data-end="1526">ğŸ“ <strong data-start="1464" data-end="1491">Structural expectations</strong> (e.g. 3-act, circular, puzzle-box)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1527" data-end="1601">
<p data-start="1529" data-end="1601">ğŸ­ <strong data-start="1532" data-end="1561">Character function shifts</strong> (hero â†” villain, love interest â†” ghost)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1602" data-end="1686">
<p data-start="1604" data-end="1686">ğŸŒ« <strong data-start="1607" data-end="1623">Mood filters</strong> (e.g. noir tone = chiaroscuro visuals, jazz + moral ambiguity)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1687" data-end="1765">
<p data-start="1689" data-end="1765">ğŸ“š <strong data-start="1692" data-end="1712">Trope insertions</strong> (e.g. Chekhovâ€™s Gun, unreliable narrator, time loop)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1766" data-end="1835">
<p data-start="1768" data-end="1835">ğŸ”„ <strong data-start="1771" data-end="1793">Thematic inversion</strong> (e.g. fate â†’ free will; love â†’ obsession)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1837" data-end="1846">ğŸ›  Tools:</p>
<ul data-start="1847" data-end="2028">
<li data-start="1847" data-end="1878">
<p data-start="1849" data-end="1878">Custom â€œgenre grammarâ€ schema</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1879" data-end="1926">
<p data-start="1881" data-end="1926">Trope ontology (TV Tropes as training corpus)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1927" data-end="1973">
<p data-start="1929" data-end="1973">Prompt templates for generative transformers</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1974" data-end="2028">
<p data-start="1976" data-end="2028">Style transfer weights (text/audio/video modalities)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2030" data-end="2033">
<h3 data-start="2035" data-end="2073">ğŸ§¬ 3. <strong data-start="2045" data-end="2073">Narrative Rewrite Engine</strong></h3>
<blockquote data-start="2075" data-end="2139">
<p data-start="2077" data-end="2139">â€œHow do we subtly realign the material to match the new mask?â€</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="2141" data-end="2221">This doesnâ€™t rewrite the whole film â€” it <strong data-start="2182" data-end="2192">nudges</strong> the meaning. Key strategies:</p>
<ul data-start="2223" data-end="2504">
<li data-start="2223" data-end="2273">
<p data-start="2225" data-end="2273">âœï¸ Rewriting voiceover/dialogue with new subtext</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2274" data-end="2317">
<p data-start="2276" data-end="2317">ğŸ¼ Re-scoring music for tonal realignment</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2318" data-end="2392">
<p data-start="2320" data-end="2392">ğŸ“º Inserting fake diegetic elements (news clips, dreams, glitch moments)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2393" data-end="2440">
<p data-start="2395" data-end="2440">ğŸŒ€ Rearranging scene order (nonlinearization)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2441" data-end="2504">
<p data-start="2443" data-end="2504">ğŸª Injecting meta moments (4th wall breaks, uncanny dialogue)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2506" data-end="2515">ğŸ›  Tools:</p>
<ul data-start="2516" data-end="2729">
<li data-start="2516" data-end="2544">
<p data-start="2518" data-end="2544">GPT-based script rewriters</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2545" data-end="2586">
<p data-start="2547" data-end="2586">TTS with voice cloning for ADR overlays</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2587" data-end="2612">
<p data-start="2589" data-end="2612">ML-based music remixers</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2613" data-end="2671">
<p data-start="2615" data-end="2671">Unity/Unreal for augmented playback + scene manipulation</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2672" data-end="2729">
<p data-start="2674" data-end="2729">Visual masking (deepfake/face-blur) for new expressions</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2731" data-end="2734">
<h3 data-start="2736" data-end="2778">ğŸŒ€ 4. <strong data-start="2746" data-end="2778">Playback &amp; Interaction Layer</strong></h3>
<blockquote data-start="2780" data-end="2814">
<p data-start="2782" data-end="2814">â€œLet the viewer tune the knobs.â€</p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="2816" data-end="2865">This is the <em data-start="2828" data-end="2847">user-facing shell</em>, where one might:</p>
<ul data-start="2867" data-end="3059">
<li data-start="2867" data-end="2918">
<p data-start="2869" data-end="2918">Select filters (e.g. <code data-start="2890" data-end="2901">SPC t m h</code> = â€œhorror modeâ€)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2919" data-end="2947">
<p data-start="2921" data-end="2947">Toggle trope overlays live</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2948" data-end="3006">
<p data-start="2950" data-end="3006">Adjust <strong data-start="2957" data-end="2968">tension</strong>, <strong data-start="2970" data-end="2983">absurdity</strong>, <strong data-start="2985" data-end="3000">romanticism</strong>, etc.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3007" data-end="3059">
<p data-start="3009" data-end="3059">Allow for branching (choose-your-own thematic arc)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3061" data-end="3070">ğŸ›  Tools:</p>
<ul data-start="3071" data-end="3239">
<li data-start="3071" data-end="3104">
<p data-start="3073" data-end="3104">Electron or web-based front-end</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3105" data-end="3132">
<p data-start="3107" data-end="3132">WebGL for visual overlays</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3133" data-end="3185">
<p data-start="3135" data-end="3185">Real-time LLM for generating context-aware content</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3186" data-end="3239">
<p data-start="3188" data-end="3239">Trope slider interface (â€œHow tragic? How surreal?â€)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3241" data-end="3244">
<h2 data-start="3246" data-end="3271">ğŸ§ª EXAMPLE WALKTHROUGH</h2>
<p data-start="3273" data-end="3335"><strong data-start="3273" data-end="3282">Input</strong>: A romcom<br data-start="3292" data-end="3295">
<strong data-start="3295" data-end="3305">Filter</strong>: <code data-start="3307" data-end="3318">SPC t m h</code> (Make it horror)</p>
<p data-start="3337" data-end="3348"><strong data-start="3337" data-end="3347">Result</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="3349" data-end="3589">
<li data-start="3349" data-end="3394">
<p data-start="3351" data-end="3394">Dialogue is re-scored with ominous strings.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3395" data-end="3440">
<p data-start="3397" data-end="3440">Color grading shifts to greenish grayscale.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3441" data-end="3490">
<p data-start="3443" data-end="3490">The quirky best friend disappears mysteriously.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3491" data-end="3548">
<p data-start="3493" data-end="3548">A benign â€œmeet-cuteâ€ becomes an unsettling coincidence.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3549" data-end="3589">
<p data-start="3551" data-end="3589">Ending becomes ambiguous or recursive.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3591" data-end="3594">
<h2 data-start="3596" data-end="3645">âš–ï¸ Challenges (and why itâ€™s â€œtoo complicatedâ€)</h2>
<ul data-start="3647" data-end="4017">
<li data-start="3647" data-end="3766">
<p data-start="3649" data-end="3766"><strong data-start="3649" data-end="3671">Semantic fragility</strong>: Story meaning is <em data-start="3690" data-end="3698">subtle</em>. Rewriting can easily break character consistency or thematic tone.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3767" data-end="3849">
<p data-start="3769" data-end="3849"><strong data-start="3769" data-end="3786">Data scarcity</strong>: No large open dataset of films with deep semantic annotation.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3850" data-end="3937">
<p data-start="3852" data-end="3937"><strong data-start="3852" data-end="3872">Compositionality</strong>: Tropes donâ€™t just stack â€” they interfere and mutate each other.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3938" data-end="4017">
<p data-start="3940" data-end="4017"><strong data-start="3940" data-end="3962">Rendering fidelity</strong>: Changing visuals convincingly is still hard at scale.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4019" data-end="4025">But...</p>
<hr data-start="4027" data-end="4030">
<h2 data-start="4032" data-end="4071">ğŸ§­ Minimal Viable Thought Experiment</h2>
<p data-start="4073" data-end="4108">You <em data-start="4077" data-end="4084">could</em> build a prototype that:</p>
<ul data-start="4109" data-end="4266">
<li data-start="4109" data-end="4132">
<p data-start="4111" data-end="4132">Ingests a film script</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4133" data-end="4172">
<p data-start="4135" data-end="4172">Rewrites scenes to shift genre/tropes</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4173" data-end="4205">
<p data-start="4175" data-end="4205">Uses TTS to generate voiceover</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4206" data-end="4266">
<p data-start="4208" data-end="4266">Plays over a storyboard, or re-edits public domain footage</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4268" data-end="4334">Like a <strong data-start="4275" data-end="4297">narrative stylizer</strong> rather than a full film transformer.</p>
