<p data-start="2858" data-end="3031">You get a compact keystroke trail that tells you roughly <em data-start="2915" data-end="2959">how to â€œplayâ€ The Matrixâ€™s narrative style</em> â€” and you can remix or reverse this to create new stories in that vein.</p>
<hr data-start="3033" data-end="3036">
<h3 data-start="3038" data-end="3059">6. <strong data-start="3045" data-end="3059">Next Steps</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="3061" data-end="3413">
<li data-start="3061" data-end="3123">
<p data-start="3063" data-end="3123">Design a <strong data-start="3072" data-end="3097">trope vector ontology</strong> aligned with your keymap.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3124" data-end="3173">
<p data-start="3126" data-end="3173">Train a classifier or prompt LLMs to tag media.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3174" data-end="3252">
<p data-start="3176" data-end="3252">Develop an algorithm to translate trope vectors back to keystroke sequences.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3253" data-end="3323">
<p data-start="3255" data-end="3323">Prototype with a small corpus (e.g. classic films or short stories).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3324" data-end="3413">
<p data-start="3326" data-end="3413">Build a UI that visualizes trope fingerprints and lets users explore â€œnarrative space.â€</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3415" data-end="3418">
<p data-start="3420" data-end="3450">If you want, I can help draft:</p>
<ul data-start="3452" data-end="3652">
<li data-start="3452" data-end="3509">
<p data-start="3454" data-end="3509">A sample trope vector schema aligned to your keystrokes</p>
