></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full" dir="auto" data-testid="conversation-turn-32" data-scroll-anchor="false"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT dijo:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto py-5 [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @[37rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @[72rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:32rem] @[34rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @[64rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto flex max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 text-base gap-4 md:gap-5 lg:gap-6 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden" tabindex="-1"><div class="group/conversation-turn relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn"><div class="relative flex-col gap-1 md:gap-3"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="ec5f9598-07fa-4b83-979d-26773fe269b8" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-4-1-mini"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark"><p data-start="0" data-end="172">Got it â€” you want a <strong data-start="20" data-end="77">keyboard-driven, trigger-and-hotkey-focused interface</strong>, not a mouse-driven node graph or drag-and-drop. Letâ€™s pivot and design a concept centered on:</p>
<ul data-start="174" data-end="337">
<li data-start="174" data-end="200">
<p data-start="176" data-end="200"><strong data-start="176" data-end="200">Nested key sequences</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="201" data-end="226">
<p data-start="203" data-end="226"><strong data-start="203" data-end="226">Contextual triggers</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="227" data-end="279">
<p data-start="229" data-end="279"><strong data-start="229" data-end="279">Real-time feedback through minimal UI elements</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="280" data-end="337">
<p data-start="282" data-end="337"><strong data-start="282" data-end="337">Fluid, fast navigation without leaving the keyboard</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="339" data-end="342">
<h1 data-start="344" data-end="406">Keyboard-Centric Interface for Trope Latent Space Navigation</h1>
<h3 data-start="408" data-end="434">1. <strong data-start="415" data-end="434">Core Principles</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="436" data-end="964">
<li data-start="436" data-end="536">
<p data-start="438" data-end="536"><strong data-start="438" data-end="463">Hierarchical keymaps:</strong> Like Spacemacs or Vim, keystrokes are nested combos (e.g., <code data-start="523" data-end="534">SPC t g h</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="537" data-end="668">
<p data-start="539" data-end="668"><strong data-start="539" data-end="560">Stateful context:</strong> The interface remembers the current â€œtrope configuration stateâ€ and adjusts available commands accordingly.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="669" data-end="776">
<p data-start="671" data-end="776"><strong data-start="671" data-end="699">Minimal visual feedback:</strong> Small overlay or status line showing current trope vector or active filters.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="777" data-end="866">
<p data-start="779" data-end="866"><strong data-start="779" data-end="800">Instant triggers:</strong> Certain keys trigger immediate trope shifts or narrative filters.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="867" data-end="964">
<p data-start="869" data-end="964"><strong data-start="869" data-end="882">Chaining:</strong> You can chain sequences to combine effects or build complex trope configurations.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="966" data-end="969">
<h3 data-start="971" data-end="1006">2. <strong data-start="978" data-end="1006">Example Keymap Structure</strong></h3>
