<hr data-start="1764" data-end="1767">
<h3 data-start="1769" data-end="1808">3. <strong data-start="1776" data-end="1808">How triggers &amp; chaining work</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="1810" data-end="2159">
<li data-start="1810" data-end="1910">
<p data-start="1812" data-end="1910">After pressing <code data-start="1827" data-end="1834">SPC t</code> to enter trope mode, subsequent keys refine the trope vector incrementally.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1911" data-end="2012">
<p data-start="1913" data-end="2012">Each keypress <strong data-start="1927" data-end="1953">applies a vector shift</strong> in latent trope space (adding or adjusting trope weights).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2013" data-end="2105">
<p data-start="2015" data-end="2105">Some keys are <strong data-start="2029" data-end="2048">toggle triggers</strong> â€” e.g., pressing <code data-start="2066" data-end="2069">b</code> toggles â€œbreak fourth wallâ€ on/off.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2106" data-end="2159">
<p data-start="2108" data-end="2159">Chaining allows combining shifts before committing.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2161" data-end="2164">
