<ul data-start="2398" data-end="2592">
<li data-start="2398" data-end="2468">
<p data-start="2400" data-end="2468">When a key is pressed, this updates instantly to show the new state.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2469" data-end="2592">
<p data-start="2471" data-end="2592">Optionally, a <strong data-start="2485" data-end="2519">mini â€œnarrative snippetâ€ panel</strong> can pop up with a one-line story summary reflecting current trope state.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2594" data-end="2597">
<h3 data-start="2599" data-end="2626">5. <strong data-start="2606" data-end="2626">Workflow example</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="2628" data-end="3012">
<li data-start="2628" data-end="2663">
<p data-start="2630" data-end="2663">User watches film or reads story.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2664" data-end="2714">
<p data-start="2666" data-end="2714">User presses <code data-start="2679" data-end="2690">SPC t g s</code> to set genre to Sci-Fi.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2715" data-end="2764">
<p data-start="2717" data-end="2764">User adds <code data-start="2727" data-end="2738">SPC t a h</code> to set archetype to Hero.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2765" data-end="2832">
<p data-start="2767" data-end="2832">User toggles meta mode with <code data-start="2795" data-end="2806">SPC t x b</code> to break the fourth wall.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2833" data-end="2939">
<p data-start="2835" data-end="2939">Each keypress shifts the latent trope vector; system updates narrative style or offers alternate scenes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2940" data-end="3012">
<p data-start="2942" data-end="3012">User can quickly undo last keystroke with <code data-start="2984" data-end="2987">u</code> or reset with <code data-start="3002" data-end="3011">SPC t r</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3014" data-end="3017">
<h3 data-start="3019" data-end="3044">6. <strong data-start="3026" data-end="3044">Advanced ideas</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="3046" data-end="3338">
<li data-start="3046" data-end="3177">
<p data-start="3048" data-end="3177"><strong data-start="3048" data-end="3076">Context-sensitive menus:</strong> If user starts typing <code data-start="3099" data-end="3108">SPC t p</code>, interface displays (via keyboard hints) available plot device keys.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3178" data-end="3278">
<p data-start="3180" data-end="3278"><strong data-start="3180" data-end="3207">Multi-key chord combos:</strong> Allow pressing multiple keys simultaneously for combined trope shifts.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3279" data-end="3338">
<p data-start="3281" data-end="3338"><strong data-start="3281" data-end="3292">Macros:</strong> Save sequences of trope keystrokes for reuse.</p>
</li>
