xt-token-text-primary w-full" dir="auto" data-testid="conversation-turn-34" data-scroll-anchor="true"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT dijo:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto py-5 [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @[37rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @[72rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:32rem] @[34rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @[64rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto flex max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 text-base gap-4 md:gap-5 lg:gap-6 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden" tabindex="-1"><div class="group/conversation-turn relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn"><div class="relative flex-col gap-1 md:gap-3"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="29951847-4ef6-4fd5-b3af-b4f96e2dc2a8" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-4-1-mini"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark"><p data-start="0" data-end="68">Hereâ€™s a list summarizing all the main topics weâ€™ve discussed today:</p>
<ol data-start="70" data-end="2450">
<li data-start="70" data-end="221">
<p data-start="73" data-end="122"><strong data-start="73" data-end="120">Movies reacting to external diegetic sounds</strong></p>
<ul data-start="126" data-end="221">
<li data-start="126" data-end="221">
<p data-start="128" data-end="221">Screen visuals or music syncing dynamically to ambient sounds (e.g., car driving by outside).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="223" data-end="382">
<p data-start="226" data-end="285"><strong data-start="226" data-end="283">Movies changing based on viewer presence or attention</strong></p>
<ul data-start="289" data-end="382">
<li data-start="289" data-end="382">
<p data-start="291" data-end="382">More action or plot if someone enters the room; filler or mundane scenes if no one watches.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="384" data-end="520">
<p data-start="387" data-end="441"><strong data-start="387" data-end="439">User interaction with movies via keyboard inputs</strong></p>
<ul data-start="445" data-end="520">
<li data-start="445" data-end="520">
<p data-start="447" data-end="520">Influencing genre, plot points, or narrative style by keystroke commands.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="522" data-end="698">
<p data-start="525" data-end="600"><strong data-start="525" data-end="598">Spacemacs-style nested keymap interfaces for trope category selection</strong></p>
<ul data-start="604" data-end="698">
<li data-start="604" data-end="698">
<p data-start="606" data-end="698">Designing hierarchical key sequences to choose genres, archetypes, plot devices, meta modes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="700" data-end="841">
<p data-start="703" data-end="773"><strong data-start="703" data-end="771">Movies breaking the fourth wall triggered by specific keystrokes</strong></p>
<ul data-start="777" data-end="841">
<li data-start="777" data-end="841">
<p data-start="779" data-end="841">Including meta commentary like reminders or personal messages.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="843" data-end="1001">
<p data-start="846" data-end="925"><strong data-start="846" data-end="923">Thinking of narrative control as genre or style filters on existing films</strong></p>
<ul data-start="929" data-end="1001">
<li data-start="929" data-end="1001">
<p data-start="931" data-end="1001">Alternate endings or style transfer filters controlled via keystrokes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1003" data-end="1146">
<p data-start="1006" data-end="1057"><strong data-start="1006" data-end="1055">Concept of a latent trope configuration space</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1061" data-end="1146">
<li data-start="1061" data-end="1146">
<p data-start="1063" data-end="1146">Representing media as points or trajectories in high-dimensional trope/style space.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1148" data-end="1301">
<p data-start="1151" data-end="1210"><strong data-start="1151" data-end="1208">Keystrokes as vector operations in latent trope space</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1214" data-end="1301">
<li data-start="1214" data-end="1301">
<p data-start="1216" data-end="1301">Moving the narrative configuration through the trope space by applying vector shifts.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1303" data-end="1451">
<p data-start="1306" data-end="1379"><strong data-start="1306" data-end="1377">Challenges of mapping tropes and media to keystrokes and vice versa</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1383" data-end="1451">
<li data-start="1383" data-end="1451">
<p data-start="1385" data-end="1451">Complex hierarchical, temporal, and multi-modal narrative aspects.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1453" data-end="1616">
<p data-start="1457" data-end="1541"><strong data-start="1457" data-end="1539">Exploration of latent spaces through force-directed graphs and vector chaining</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1546" data-end="1616">
<li data-start="1546" data-end="1616">
<p data-start="1548" data-end="1616">Visualization and navigation making complex latent spaces intuitive.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1618" data-end="1792">
<p data-start="1622" data-end="1697"><strong data-start="1622" data-end="1695">Designing an interactive visual interface for trope space exploration</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1702" data-end="1792">
<li data-start="1702" data-end="1792">
<p data-start="1704" data-end="1792">Initial ideas for node-based graph visualization, drag-and-drop, and timeline scrubbing.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1794" data-end="1960">
<p data-start="1798" data-end="1872"><strong data-start="1798" data-end="1870">Refinement to a keyboard-centric, trigger-and-hotkey-based interface</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1877" data-end="1960">
<li data-start="1877" data-end="1960">
<p data-start="1879" data-end="1960">Nested key sequences, stateful trope mode, minimal UI feedback, instant triggers.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1962" data-end="2135">
<p data-start="1966" data-end="2037"><strong data-start="1966" data-end="2035">Detailed keymap tree examples for trope categories and meta modes</strong></p>
<ul data-start="2042" data-end="2135">
<li data-start="2042" data-end="2135">
